# THE LDRAW PARTS THE APPLICATION CAN DRAW ARE TRACKED ON PURPOSE - do not "clean" them out.
# Sangala Blocks draws every part from its real LDraw geometry, so a part that is not in this
# folder cannot be drawn at all: the bridge returns an empty file and the page silently falls back
# to a hand-drawn stand-in shape. That is exactly what happened before 2026-08-28, when only 39
# part files were tracked - every primitive was here, but the parts that assemble them were not,
# so a curved bow came out a plain box on any machine but the one that built the folder.
#
# What travels: every part the application can represent, plus the closure of everything those
# parts reference. 9,582 files. Regenerate the list rather than editing it by hand:
#     python tools\ship_parts.py > parts-to-ship.txt
#     git add -f --pathspec-from-file=parts-to-ship.txt
#
# Everything ELSE under LDraw stays out - the other 19,000 parts the application has no shape for,
# and the 145 MB archive. Re-fetch that with:
#   curl -sL -o LDraw/complete.zip https://library.ldraw.org/library/updates/complete.zip
LDraw/

# The generated ship list is a build artifact, not source
parts-to-ship.txt

# Python bytecode from the tools scripts
__pycache__/

# A standalone diagnostic copy of the application - superseded by Projects/Blank Workspace.block
Projects/Blank Workspace (Ver 1.0).html

# Snapshot and document output written while testing - not source
Documents/Test File.docx
Documents/Test snapshots.docx
Projects/test.ldr
Projects/test.png
tools/designnum_table.json

# ARCHIVE FOLDERS DO NOT BELONG IN A REPOSITORY. Git already holds every prior version of every
# tracked file - that is what it is for - so an Archive inside it stores the old versions twice.
# Archive is a Dropbox idea, for folders that have no history of their own. 81 files and ~38 MB
# across the three repositories were tracked this way before 2026-08-30. The folders stay on disk;
# they are simply not carried.
Archive/
.Archive/

# Word exports of documents that are themselves tracked. The .docx is the source; a PDF beside it
# is regenerated from Word whenever it is wanted, so carrying both stores the same document twice.
Documents/Crane Snapshots 2.pdf
Documents/Crane snapshots.pdf
